  "term": "wub",
  "says": "The dubstep wobble: a bass whose low-pass cutoff is swept by a tempo-synced LFO at an eighth or a sixteenth, resonance high enough that the sweep is heard as a vowel, drive or clipping after the filter for grit, a clean sine sub underneath routed around the filter. The signature is a large periodic BRIGHTNESS movement at the LFO's rate (a few Hz) on a low fundamental. Measured 2026-09-13: with the clipper and the compressor the LEVEL barely moves (0.29 dB over the held note) while the centroid swings by semitones - the first version of this entry expected a level movement of 3 dB and was refuted; the wobble is a brightness movement.",
